Z||000005||Cooter||05-08-2001||11:29 PM||||If they are the same length and diminsions as the manifolds, they CAN be MADE to work- if you are good friends with the man at the muffler shop. You will loose the Y-pipe, the front bank will have a muffler that goes where the converter used to be and exits on the right side of the car. The rear bank will have a muffler in the stock location and exit on the left side of the car. A 60 degree engine with true duals has a rather unique sound to it.||||reg||1
